<% layout("layouts/boilerplate") -%>

<main class="py-4 py-lg-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <article class="col-lg-9 col-xl-8">
            <header class="mb-4 pb-3 border-bottom">
                <p class="text-danger fw-semibold text-uppercase small mb-2">Legal</p>
                <h1 class="display-6 fw-semibold mb-2">Terms and conditions</h1>
                <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">Last updated: October 12, 2026</p>
            </header>

            <div class="alert alert-light border" role="note">
                Heavenly is an independent learning project and is not affiliated with Airbnb. This version helps people discover stays; it does not take bookings or payments.
            </div>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">1. Using Heavenly</h2>
                <p>These terms apply when you browse or use the Heavenly website. The site lets people search and filter accommodation listings, view locations on a map, create listings, save stays to an account, and post reviews. By using these features, you agree to follow these terms and applicable law.</p>
                <p>Heavenly does not currently provide reservations, availability confirmation, payment processing, guest-host messaging, insurance, or dispute resolution. A listing is informational only; it is not a booking offer or confirmation. Do not send money or sensitive payment details through this site.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">2. Accounts</h2>
                <p>You are responsible for keeping your login details private and for activity performed through your account. Provide accurate account information and tell the site operator if you believe someone has accessed your account without permission. Account features such as creating a listing, saving a stay, and writing a review require sign-in.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">3. Listings and hosting</h2>
                <p>If you publish a listing, you must have permission to offer the place and to use its photos and other materials. Keep descriptions, prices, and location details truthful and lawful. You are responsible for the content you submit and for checking that it complies with rules that apply to you and the property.</p>
                <p>Listings and map locations are supplied by users and may be incomplete, inaccurate, or out of date. A map pin is a guide, not a guarantee of an exact address or the suitability, safety, or availability of a place.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">4. Reviews and other content</h2>
                <p>You keep ownership of content you submit. You give Heavenly permission to store, display, and process it as needed to operate this project, including showing listing photos, descriptions, public reviews, and the username associated with a listing or review. Do not upload content you do not have the right to use, private information about another person, or abusive, deceptive, or unlawful material.</p>
                <p>Reviews should describe a genuine experience and be relevant to the listing. The site operator may remove content that violates these terms or applicable law.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">5. Acceptable use</h2>
                <p>Do not use Heavenly to break the law, interfere with the site, bypass security, distribute malicious code, mislead other users, or collect information through scraping or automated access without permission. Do not impersonate another person or misuse another member’s account or content.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">6. Third-party services</h2>
                <p>Maps and address lookup are provided through Mapbox. Default listing photos load from Unsplash URLs stored in MongoDB Atlas, while photos uploaded by hosts are stored through Cloudinary. Those services have their own terms and privacy practices. Links or sharing controls may also take you to social networks; Heavenly does not control those services.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">7. Availability and responsibility</h2>
                <p>This learning project is provided as available and may change, be interrupted, or contain errors. To the extent permitted by law, the site operator does not guarantee that listings or map information are accurate or that the site will always be available. Nothing in these terms removes rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h4">8. Changes and questions</h2>
                <p>These terms may be updated as the project changes. The updated date will appear at the top of this page. For questions about these terms, contact the person or team operating the Heavenly deployment.</p>
                <p class="mb-0">Read the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> to learn how account, listing, and review information is handled.</p>
            </section>
        </article>
    </div>
</main>
